  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499437346611_995960_29661" xmi:uuid="4bc9ad31-9cde-4fd9-a8a9-5fe3b34a7122" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510148032819_477826_31012" xmi:uuid="f5e3dd7d-faf6-4002-a912-85c8fb6caab4" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499437346611_995960_29661"/>
      <body>This capability specifies the information needed to describe the association between original product or engineering information and changed product or engineering information. The changed product or engineering information is based upon the original product or engineering information. A delta exchange implies an exchange of differences with respect to a set of data previously sent. That means it is the exchange of results of activities, which have been performed at the sender’s side and are to be communicated. &lt;example&gt;Typical activities are "add component 3 and 4 to an assembly", "remove document xyz from the set of describing documents of a part", "modify requirement x".&lt;/example&gt;The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;DeltaChange_domainModel_Overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 delta change Domain model&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <name>DeltaChange</name>
