    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193065_811265_23507" xmi:uuid="a65f68ca-e136-4a22-9ff9-a026f5667020" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454506281520_578238_43368" xmi:uuid="e27120d5-bc2a-4922-b5d4-6e300c995dee" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193065_811265_23507"/>
        <body>A DeleteElement is a type of DeltaChangeActivity that identifies one or several objects that have been deleted. &lt;example&gt;Version A of a part has a subcomponent C1. In version B of the part this subcomponent is deleted. This change can be described by referencing with the attribute PreviousDesignObject of DeleteElement an Occurrence representing the deleted subcomponent C1 in version A. The DeleteElement object is referenced by a DeltaChange object via ChangeActivities. Finally, DeltaChange is referencing (via DescribedChange) a PartVersionRelationship where the relating PartVersion represents version A of the part.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>DeleteElement</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193570_848699_26047" xmi:uuid="473e752f-c3d7-40bf-b77e-cf5aae687762" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
